  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Feasibility Study - Potable Water Filtration Project, through Government of Mexico</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The State of Durango Potable Water Filtration Pilot Project Feasibility Study is enabling the Water Commission of the State of Durango to assess the deployment of point-of-use water treatment units to address drinking water needs in the Mexican State of Durango. USTDA is providing a grant in the amount of $343,952 to the State Water Commission of Durango to partially fund the cost of the $687,903 feasibility study.</narrative>
  </description>
